WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:02.902
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show,"
everybody. I'm Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.570
Thank you so much for tuning in.
I appreciate it.

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:06.873
There's a lot of important news
we got to get to,

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:08.474
so let's get to the monologue.

00:00:08.474 --> 00:00:10.209
But first,
we have a great show tonight.

00:00:10.209 --> 00:00:11.744
Robert De Niro is here,

00:00:11.744 --> 00:00:14.747
Oscar-winning film legend
Robert De Niro.

00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:17.016
He's doing something cool
with his Tribeca Film Festival,

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:19.952
which had to be moved
because of the pandemic.

00:00:19.952 --> 00:00:24.090
He has now a new idea
that Jane Rosenthal came up with

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.559
which is drive-ins,

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:28.227
Tribeca drive-in movies.

00:00:28.227 --> 00:00:31.063
It's a great idea. I'm going
to talk to him about that.

00:00:31.063 --> 00:00:37.170
Then James Blake, tennis legend
and also best-selling author,

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:41.607
talks about his experience
with mistaken identity

00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:44.577
and his experience
with the police

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.613
that happened a few years ago
in New York.

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:48.381
Do you remember that, honey?
-Mm-hmm, yeah.

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:50.249
-Yeah. It's wild.

00:00:50.249 --> 00:00:52.352
His story is insane.

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:55.088
So I'm happy that he came on the
show to talk to me about that.

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:59.792
And then one of my all-time
favorites, honey, yours, too,

00:00:59.792 --> 00:01:03.429
our pal Lenny Kravitz is closing
out the show tonight with his --

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:04.730
Come on.
-Classic.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:06.432
-Can you get cooler
than Lenny Kravitz?

00:01:06.432 --> 00:01:07.934
Can you get cooler?

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:09.902
-I think his daughter,
but that's it.

00:01:09.902 --> 00:01:11.571
-Yeah, she's cool.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:12.805
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:12.805 --> 00:01:15.808
But he is so cool.
-It runs in the family.

00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:17.476
-Gosh. He's one of those guys

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:20.980
where it's like,
you can give him a wardrobe

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:23.649
and me the same exact wardrobe,

00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:27.119
and you'll see the extreme
of "Who wore it better?"

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:30.456
It's like,
he can just do it, man.

00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:32.291
You could put a dollhouse

00:01:32.291 --> 00:01:34.059
and say, "Dude, make that
into something cool."

00:01:34.059 --> 00:01:35.829
He'll just, like, hold it.
He'll hold --

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:37.730
I'm just looking at a dollhouse,

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.832
'cause we have dollhouses
all over the house.

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:42.268
But anyways,
he is just the best --

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:46.239
Anyways, he's doing the song
"Believe" tonight,

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:48.741
which is great,
and I appreciate him doing that.

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:51.043
I do love Lenny Kravitz.

00:01:51.043 --> 00:01:53.579
Guys, let's get to
some news here.

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:56.715
Well, guys, apparently
the long-running TV show "Cops"

00:01:56.715 --> 00:01:59.285
which many people have
considered racist,

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:01.620
has just been canceled.

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:03.789
So now if you want to watch
a bunch of drunk people

00:02:03.789 --> 00:02:07.260
embarrass themselves, you'll
have to watch "The Bachelor"

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:11.697
or "Real Housewives"
or "Below Deck"

00:02:11.697 --> 00:02:13.700
or "Below Deck: Med"

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.236
or "Below Deck Sail--"
No, just kidding.

00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:18.204
Most people are glad
"Cops" has been canceled,

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:19.405
although it's tough news

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:21.708
for stoners who love watching
shirtless guys

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:25.044
try to fail to hop a fence.

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:26.479
"Cops" was a crazy show.

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:28.614
It actually had more
naked and afraid people

00:02:28.614 --> 00:02:31.818
than "Naked and Afraid."

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:33.819
"Cops" first aired in 1989,

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:36.856
but really, they just aired the
same three episodes for 30 years

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:39.192
and nobody noticed.

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:41.227
It's not just TV shows
that are being canceled.

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:44.397
Some movies are being removed
from streaming platforms

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:47.834
until they can return
with historical context.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:50.369 line:0%
-This morning,
an American cinema classic,

00:02:50.369 --> 00:02:52.905 line:0%
"Gone with the Wind,"
has been temporarily pulled

00:02:52.905 --> 00:02:55.441 line:0%
by the streaming platform
HBO Max.

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:58.110 line:0%
For years, the movie has been
considered controversial

00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:59.879 line:0%
for its depiction
of black people

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:02.482 line:0%
and its glorification
of slavery.

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:04.717
-A lot of conservatives
were upset,

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:05.851
to which everyone else said,

00:03:05.851 --> 00:03:09.288
"Frankly, my dear,
I don't give a damn."

00:03:09.288 --> 00:03:11.157
To anyone who is upset,

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:15.695
really? You're going to watch
a four-hour movie from 1939

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:18.097
this weekend? That's what
you're planning on doing?

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:20.433
You had the whole time
during the quarantine.

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:22.835
But this weekend is when
you were going to watch

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:25.938
"Gone with the Wind"?

00:03:25.938 --> 00:03:27.473
In the meantime,
if you still want to watch

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:30.409
something super offensive,
"Cats" is available on demand.

00:03:30.409 --> 00:03:32.478
No, that's -- Come on.

00:03:36.615 --> 00:03:38.084
Yep, by pulling the film,

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:41.487
HBO Max accomplished
something very important --

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:44.056
They got people
to talk about HBO Max.

00:03:44.056 --> 00:03:46.659
And what actually is it?

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:48.594
Meanwhile, Quibi is so desperate
for attention,

00:03:48.594 --> 00:03:50.229
they were like, "We'll take it.

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:53.800
We're going to break it up into
300 parts."

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.334
And it's not just entertainment.

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:57.803
Now businesses are also dealing
with these issues,

00:03:57.803 --> 00:03:59.572
some better than others.

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:03.209
-CrossFit CEO Greg Glassman
has resigned after outrage

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:06.012
over a controversial post
about George Floyd.

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:09.381
A tweet Saturday linked
Floyd's death to the pandemic.

00:04:09.381 --> 00:04:12.218
-Yeah, the CEO of CrossFit
stepped down.

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:15.455
Actually, first, he stepped up
and then down and then up again,

00:04:15.455 --> 00:04:18.958
then down, then up, and then
he stepped down finally.

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:21.594
Then when he left the building,
instead of driving off,

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:26.298
he just flipped
a giant tire home.

00:04:26.298 --> 00:04:28.100
What was he thinking?

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:32.739
He mocked the protests and
the coronavirus in one tweet.

00:04:32.739 --> 00:04:34.207
He shouldn't be
the CEO of CrossFit.

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:37.910
He should be the president
of the United States.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:40.646
Yep, he hit coronavirus
and police brutality.

00:04:40.646 --> 00:04:42.348
He just needs to weigh in
on gender,

00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:46.285
and he'll finish the triathlon
of offending people.

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:48.287
Well, it seems like
things are slowly changing.

00:04:48.287 --> 00:04:50.289
In fact, the Army says
that it might rename

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:52.558
forts that are named after
Confederate officers

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:55.127
like Fort Bragg and Fort Hood.

00:04:55.127 --> 00:04:57.796
Yeah, they want new names
that everyone can get behind,

00:04:57.796 --> 00:05:00.732
so they did a poll on
what Americans love right now,

00:05:00.732 --> 00:05:02.968
and I think they solved
their problem. Take a look.

00:05:02.968 --> 00:05:06.672 line:0%
Fort Bragg is being renamed
Fort Free Guac.

00:05:06.672 --> 00:05:08.941 line:0%
Fort Hood is changing to

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:11.010 line:0%
Fort Coming Up With
A Good Comeback In The Moment,

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:14.079 line:0%
And Not In The Shower
The Next Day.

00:05:14.079 --> 00:05:15.981 line:0%
Fort Benning will be

00:05:15.981 --> 00:05:20.386 line:0%
Fort Getting The Capri-Sun Straw
Into The Pouch On The First Try.

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:25.123 line:0%
And finally, Fort Pickett
will be Fort BTS.

00:05:25.123 --> 00:05:26.392
Let's see how that works.

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:27.860
A lot of people are saying

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:31.564
the only way to achieve racial
justice is to go out and vote.

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:32.932
But take a look at what happened

00:05:32.932 --> 00:05:35.568
when people tried to vote
in Georgia yesterday.

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:39.037
-Georgia's election
is being called a catastrophe,

00:05:39.037 --> 00:05:41.640
particularly in
largely minority areas.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:44.309
The Secretary of State
is opening an investigation

00:05:44.309 --> 00:05:48.114
after reports of long waits,
voting machines not working,

00:05:48.114 --> 00:05:51.350
and a lack of ballots
in some areas.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:53.352
-You know you did a bad job
with your election

00:05:53.352 --> 00:05:56.321
when you make Iowa's election
look good.

00:05:56.321 --> 00:05:57.757
Seriously, it's not a good sign

00:05:57.757 --> 00:05:59.758
when "The Masked Singer" is
better at running an election

00:05:59.758 --> 00:06:01.560
than an entire state.

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:02.728
And finally, everybody,

00:06:02.728 --> 00:06:05.130
hopefully this might
lift up your spirits.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:07.900
The Dalai Lama
is actually releasing an album

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:11.504
featuring some of his teachings
and mantras set to music.

00:06:11.504 --> 00:06:13.739
And actually,
he even released a song

00:06:13.739 --> 00:06:16.375
to help people deal with what's
going on in the world right now.

00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:17.709
Let's take a listen.

00:06:17.709 --> 00:06:21.514
[ Man screaming,
heavy metal music playing ]

00:06:21.514 --> 00:06:23.215
Alright, stop, stop. That's --

00:06:23.215 --> 00:06:25.351
Are we sure
that's the right song?

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:28.221
I mean, we're in a quarantine,
so the producers --

00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:30.390
Anyway, we're doing what we can.

